# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is git-ignored.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     $EDITOR .env
#
# WHY renvor DOES NOT WRITE `.env` FOR YOU: doing so would mean inventing a credential and
# persisting it, then either printing it or leaving it silently on disk. Every value below is
# EMPTY on purpose, and every one is read by the application from the environment ONLY — none is
# in a file this project ships, a manifest, a log line, or a URL.

# The database connection string, credential included (framework limitation 010/L-15, retained in
# Phase 011: the persistence layer takes a URL). Read once, by the database provider, at Boot;
# never logged.
RENVOR_DATABASE_URL=
